// Logic program 1: (AA OR 0F) AND 3C = 2C. Operands share bits, so OR, XOR and ADD give different results.
20 // 00: LDA 80 - load AA
80
40 // 02: OR  81 - AA OR 0F = AF (XOR would give A5, ADD B9)
81
50 // 04: AND 82 - AF AND 3C = 2C (pass-through would give 3C)
82
10 // 06: STA 83
83
f0 // 08: HLT - final PC is 09
